## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a simple, robust ingestion path with per-record contracts, schema normalization, and safe upserts, plus practical validation and monitoring.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight schema registry for canonical schema
- Per-record contracts via metadata and record_hash
- Upserts with MERGE into Delta Lake
- Bad_data routing for invalid records
- Late data handling with watermarking
- Basic monitoring and lineage capture

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Spark-like sketch in JS for readability
const raw = readJsonFeeds(regions);
const canonical = raw.map(r => normalize(r));
canonical.forEach(rec => {
  rec._region = rec.region;
  rec._ingest_ts = Date.now();
  rec._record_hash = sha256(JSON.stringify(rec));
});
writeDeltaLake(canonical, 'db.delta_table');
```

